{
  "duration": 49.899,
  "phrases": [
    {
      "start": 0.099,
      "end": 1.279,
      "text": "So welcome back."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.819,
      "end": 4.279,
      "text": "I hope you have gone through the theory part for this topic."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.799,
      "end": 6.279,
      "text": "Now it's time to solve some problems."
    },
    {
      "start": 6.92,
      "end": 9.019,
      "text": "Now, in this problem, we are given a right triangle."
    },
    {
      "start": 9.579,
      "end": 11.319,
      "text": "The side opposite to angle A is"
    },
    {
      "start": 11.92,
      "end": 12.96,
      "text": "nine centimeter,"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.599,
      "end": 16.519,
      "text": "and the side adjacent to angle A is 12 centimeter."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.18,
      "end": 19.76,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find the value of tan A."
    },
    {
      "start": 20.439,
      "end": 21.819,
      "text": "Now, what does tan actually mean?"
    },
    {
      "start": 22.359,
      "end": 27.599,
      "text": "For any right triangle, tan A is equal to opposite side divided by adjacent side."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.279,
      "end": 31.119,
      "text": "Now, let us put the given values into the formula."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.679,
      "end": 31.959,
      "text": "Tan"
    },
    {
      "start": 32.759,
      "end": 34.819,
      "text": "A equal to nine divided by 12."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.279,
      "end": 37.259,
      "text": "Both nine and 12 are divisible by three."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.819,
      "end": 42.619,
      "text": "After simplifying, we get tan A equal to three by four."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.139,
      "end": 43.439,
      "text": "Done."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.919,
      "end": 47.479,
      "text": "So the final answer will be three by four. Hence,"
    },
    {
      "start": 47.799,
      "end": 49.899,
      "text": "the correct option is option A."
    }
  ],
